---
import Case from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Img from '../../components/Img.astro';
const data = {
  "title": "Monocoque Magazine",
  "label": "Case Study / 04",
  "tags": [
    "Magazine Design",
    "Art Direction",
    "Branding"
  ],
  "meta": [
    [
      "Role",
      "Art Director & Designer"
    ],
    [
      "Year",
      "2022"
    ],
    [
      "Duration",
      "4 Months"
    ],
    [
      "Tools",
      "Adobe InDesign, Photoshop, Illustrator"
    ],
    [
      "Type",
      "Magazine Design"
    ]
  ],
  "cover": {
    "src": "Monocoque Magazine/MM Project Cover.jpg",
    "alt": "Monocoque Magazine"
  },
  "pageTitle": "Monocoque Magazine | Kamesh Raj Shanmugam",
  "description": "Case study: end-to-end art direction for Monocoque, an independent Formula 1 print magazine."
};
---
<Case {...data}>
<div class="project-content">
        <div class="project-body">
          <!-- Overview -->
          <section class="content-section">
            <div class="content-section-header">
              <h2 class="content-section-title">Overview</h2>
              <span class="content-section-index">01</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Monocoque is an independent Formula 1 magazine developed entirely
              from scratch, spanning audience research and editorial direction
              through to full art direction and final print-ready layouts. The
              project encompassed every stage of magazine creation: defining the
              readership, establishing the brand, setting an editorial mandate,
              and producing the final designs including a cover, table of
              contents, feature spread, subscription page, and web ads.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- The Brand -->
          <section class="content-section">
            <div class="content-section-header">
              <h2 class="content-section-title">The Brand</h2>
              <span class="content-section-index">02</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              <em>Monocoque</em> is a French word meaning "Single Shell",
              referring to the construction method used in Formula 1 cars where
              the body and chassis form a single structural unit. The name
              signals the magazine's core focus: the technical depth,
              engineering precision, and strategic intelligence behind the
              sport. Beyond the technical, Monocoque also covers team and driver
              performance, off-track activities, sustainability, the business
              and financial side of F1, and historic Grand Prix moments.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- Editorial Mandate -->
          <section class="content-section">
            <div class="content-section-header">
              <h2 class="content-section-title">Editorial Mandate</h2>
              <span class="content-section-index">03</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Monocoque's mission is to give readers a comprehensive,
              authoritative view of Formula 1. The magazine delivers expert
              technical analysis, exclusive photography and illustration,
              behind-the-scenes access, and interviews with key figures.
              Coverage spans current performance, iconic historical moments,
              sustainability, and the future direction of the sport, always with
              a perspective that respects the intelligence and passion of its
              readership.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- Audience Research -->
          <section class="content-section">
            <div class="content-section-header">
              <h2 class="content-section-title">Audience Research</h2>
              <span class="content-section-index">04</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Defining the readership was the first step. The target audience
              are affluent, well-educated Formula 1 enthusiasts aged 25 and
              above, forming a global demographic with an active, high-income
              lifestyle and a genuine appetite for depth and quality.
            </p>
            <div class="stat-grid">
              <div class="stat-item">
                <span class="stat-value">25+</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Age Range</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat-item">
                <span class="stat-value">80%</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Male Readership</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat-item">
                <span class="stat-value">CDN$140k+</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Median Income</span>
              </div>
              <div class="stat-item">
                <span class="stat-value">Global</span>
                <span class="stat-label">Geographic Reach</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p>
              Readers are white-collar professionals and service sector leaders.
              Their interests span exercise, reading, go-karting, collecting
              classic cars, skiing, and travel. Brand affinities include Rolex,
              Richard Mille, Mercedes, Porsche, Apple, and Louis Vuitton.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- User Persona -->
          <section class="content-section">
            <div class="content-section-header">
              <h2 class="content-section-title">User Persona</h2>
              <span class="content-section-index">05</span>
            </div>
            <div class="persona">
              <div class="persona-header">
                <div class="persona-avatar">CJ</div>
                <div>
                  <p class="persona-name">Carter Jones</p>
                  <p class="persona-role">
                    Age 45 &nbsp;·&nbsp; CEO, Fashion Brand &nbsp;·&nbsp; Monaco
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="persona-body">
                <div class="persona-col">
                  <p class="persona-col-title">About</p>
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      Passionate F1 fan since youth, attends multiple Grand Prix
                      events annually
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Owns a rare Bugatti Veyron and a collection of high-end
                      supercars
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Resides in a Monaco penthouse, just steps from the Circuit
                      de Monaco
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Active in charitable organisations and high-profile social
                      circles
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="persona-col">
                  <p class="persona-col-title">Motivation</p>
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      Reads Monocoque to stay current on F1 developments and
                      technical insights
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Values exclusive interviews with drivers and team
                      principals
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      Wants a magazine that matches his standard for quality and
                      depth
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Visual Design -->
          <section class="content-section">
            <div class="content-section-header">
              <h2 class="content-section-title">Visual Design</h2>
              <span class="content-section-index">06</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              The style guide was built around a bold, high-contrast palette
              that conveys prestige and speed. Near-black and white form the
              primary pair, with a vibrant yellow and a punchy red as accent
              colours, reflecting the drama and energy of Formula 1.
            </p>
            <div class="palette-grid">
              <div class="swatch">
                <div class="swatch-block swatch-mm-black"></div>
                <span class="swatch-label">#191818</span>
              </div>
              <div class="swatch">
                <div class="swatch-block swatch-mm-white"></div>
                <span class="swatch-label">#FFFFFF</span>
              </div>
              <div class="swatch">
                <div class="swatch-block swatch-mm-yellow"></div>
                <span class="swatch-label">#FFCB05</span>
              </div>
              <div class="swatch">
                <div class="swatch-block swatch-mm-red"></div>
                <span class="swatch-label">#E31B4D</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p>
              Typography pairs <strong>Cormorant Garamond</strong> for body
              text, lending an editorial, refined quality, paired with
              <strong>Avant Garde</strong> for headings, providing a geometric,
              modern contrast that feels at home in the world of motorsport.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- Final Designs -->
          <section class="content-section">
            <div class="content-section-header">
              <h2 class="content-section-title">Final Designs</h2>
              <span class="content-section-index">07</span>
            </div>
            <!-- 1. Cover -->
            <figure class="mag-img-single">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Cover.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Cover" />
            </figure>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Cover:</strong> The front cover of Monocoque Magazine,
              featuring the Red Bull RB18 under dramatic studio lighting.
            </p>

            <!-- 2+3. TOC -->
            <div class="mag-spread">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine TOC.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Table of Contents" />
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine TOC 2.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Table of Contents 2" />
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Table of Contents:</strong> A two-page spread organising
              content across six editorial sections, from Race Info to Off the
              Grid.
            </p>

            <!-- 4+5. Editorial 1 & 2 -->
            <div class="mag-spread">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Editorial 1.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Editorial 1" />
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Editorial 2.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Editorial 2" />
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Feature Opening:</strong> Opening spread of the Red Bull
              2022 dominance feature, pairing a full-bleed team portrait with
              pull quotes and body copy.
            </p>

            <!-- 6. Editorial 3 -->
            <figure class="mag-img-single">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Editorial 3.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Editorial 3" />
            </figure>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Feature (cont.):</strong> Continuation of the Red Bull
              article, transitioning into technical analysis supported by
              supporting photography.
            </p>

            <!-- 7+8. Editorial 4 & 5 -->
            <div class="mag-spread">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Editorial 4.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Editorial 4" />
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Editorial 5.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Editorial 5" />
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Editorial Spread:</strong> Double-page layout exploring
              engineering and design developments across the 2022 season.
            </p>

            <!-- 9+10. Editorial 6 & 7 -->
            <div class="mag-spread">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Editorial 6.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Editorial 6" />
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Editorial 7.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Editorial 7" />
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Editorial Spread:</strong> Further editorial coverage
              balancing full-bleed photography and typeset body copy in a
              structured grid.
            </p>

            <!-- 11. Editorial 8 -->
            <figure class="mag-img-single">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Editorial 8.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Editorial 8" />
            </figure>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Editorial Page:</strong> Single-page layout with a
              dramatic full-bleed photograph and minimal typographic overlay.
            </p>

            <!-- 12+13. Subscription -->
            <div class="mag-pair">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Subscription Inside.png" alt="Subscription Inside" />
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Subscription Outside.png" alt="Subscription Outside" />
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Subscription Card:</strong> Business reply mail insert and
              subscription offer, adapted from the Monocoque print identity.
            </p>

            <!-- 14+15. Web Ads -->
            <div class="mag-pair--ads">
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Web Ad Square.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Web Ad Square" />
              <Img src="Monocoque Magazine/Monocoque Magazine Web Ad Vertical.png" alt="Monocoque Magazine Web Ad Vertical" />
            </div>
            <p class="image-caption">
              <strong>Web Ads:</strong> Square and vertical digital ad formats
              adapted from the Monocoque print identity for online use.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- Reflection -->
          <section class="content-section">
            <div class="content-section-header">
              <h2 class="content-section-title">Reflection</h2>
              <span class="content-section-index">08</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Building Monocoque end-to-end made the relationship between
              research and art direction concrete. Audience interviews and the
              editorial mandate did not sit beside the layouts — they decided
              hierarchy, pacing, and how much technical depth a spread could
              carry before it stopped feeling like a magazine.
            </p>
            <p>
              The print constraint was useful. Designing for a physical
              signature forced sharper choices about cover drama, table-of-
              contents clarity, and how subscription materials should extend
              the brand without becoming generic marketing collateral.
            </p>
            <p>
              Next time I would pressure-test the persona with a broader
              reader sample, and produce a tighter production checklist for
              colour, crop marks, and ad formats so the jump from InDesign to
              print-ready files stays as intentional as the editorial voice.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>

        <!-- Sidebar -->
        <aside class="project-sidebar">
          <div class="sidebar-group">
            <p class="sidebar-group-title">Project Info</p>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-label">Type</span>
              <span class="sidebar-value">Magazine Design</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-label">Medium</span>
              <span class="sidebar-value">Print</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-label">Role</span>
              <span class="sidebar-value">Art Director &amp; Designer</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-label">Duration</span>
              <span class="sidebar-value">4 Months</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-label">Year</span>
              <span class="sidebar-value">2022</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sidebar-group">
            <p class="sidebar-group-title">Tools Used</p>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-value">Adobe InDesign</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-value">Adobe Photoshop</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-value">Adobe Illustrator</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="sidebar-group">
            <p class="sidebar-group-title">Deliverables</p>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-value">Cover Design</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-value">Table of Contents</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-value">Feature Spread</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-value">Subscription Page</span>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-item">
              <span class="sidebar-value">Web Ads</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
</Case>
